// Aeon engine demo — the game manifest: the minimal `implement` of the engine's
// Game contract (the engine-boots-without-Sonic proof). Three value bindings, no
// hook binds — the `= empty` defaults carry both hooks, so the demo installs
// nothing at boot or per-frame. This module emits nothing.
module games.demo.game

use games.demo.constants.{GS_DEMO}
// GLOB, and it is a REQUIREMENT rather than a style choice: `fold_caps()` calls
// `scene_caps()` by name, and a comptime fn's free names resolve at the CALL SITE
// (docs/EMP_PITFALLS.md §2), so every helper the fold reaches has to be visible HERE.
// A selective `use ...{fold_caps}` fails loudly with `unknown function scene_caps` —
// scene_dsl.emp's own call-site-resolution banner states the same requirement for scene
// authors ("a scene module must `use engine.level.scene_dsl.*`, never a selective use").
use engine.level.scene_dsl.*

// DEMO_SCENES — the demo's scene registry, and it is EMPTY ON PURPOSE. The demo has no
// parallax and must not acquire a dependency on it: it is the permanent
// engine-is-game-agnostic proof. An empty registry is a legitimate registry, not a
// missing one, and declaring it is what lets the mask below be DERIVED.
//
// TYPED `[Scene; 0]` rather than a bare `[]`, and the type is the length pin: a scene
// added here without moving the `0` is a type error, and the fold cannot be handed
// something that is not a scene list. It emits no bytes — a `const` is comptime, and this
// module still emits nothing.
//
// THE TYPE IS ALSO WHAT LETS A TEXT TOOL READ THIS. tools/scene_spans.py derives the
// demo's expected ZERO capability spans from this manifest, cannot evaluate comptime, and
// refuses to guess (a wrong zero there asserts the maximal elision). It follows the
// `SCANLINE_CAPS = <name>` binding below to `fold_caps(DEMO_SCENES)` and accepts `[Scene; 0]`
// as the proof the registry is empty — a declared length, checked by sigil, not this tool
// reading `[]`. Give this registry a scene and that tool REFUSES by design, naming the count.
pub const DEMO_SCENES: [Scene; 0] = []

// THE FOLD — what the registry above actually demands, computed.
//
// UNTIL 2026-09-10 THIS LINE COULD NOT BE WRITTEN AT ALL. `fold_caps()` opened with
// `ensure(scenes.len >= 1, ..)` and refused an empty registry, so this game — alone among
// the games — had a `SCANLINE_CAPS` that no check could see, and the file said so in those
// words: "Nothing to derive and nothing to verify: fold_caps() REFUSES an empty registry
// rather than folding it to 0, so the demo deliberately has no scene registry to check this
// against." That guard is gone (content-pinning audit item 0 / A6; the derivation that 0 is
// the OR-fold's identity is written at fold_caps() in engine/level/scene_dsl.emp), and the
// route-around goes with it.
pub const DemoScenes_CapsFolded = fold_caps(DEMO_SCENES)

pub implement Game {
    // No player/camera jump-lock system in the demo — the camera's inert
    // deadzone-follow arm.
    const CAMERA_JUMP_LOCK = false

    // No authored scenes, so the fold above is 0 — both the honest value and the maximal
    // specialisation (P2 may drop every scanline service here).
    //
    // DERIVED, not declared, and that makes this game the FIRST whose mask is. Read
    // engine/system/game_contract.emp's banner for this member and note the gap it
    // describes: "Derived-and-verified, never hand-maintained-unchecked … an ensure there
    // proves the fold is a SUBSET of this declaration." games/sonic4 satisfies the SECOND
    // half — it writes `SCANLINE_CAPS = $0FDE` by hand and its registry checks the fold
    // against it. Nobody satisfied the first half, and the demo satisfied neither, because
    // the mechanism refused to run on an empty registry at all. Binding the fold itself is
    // the stronger of the two shapes: a subset test can be passed by a declaration that is
    // merely wide enough, while this cannot be wrong.
    const SCANLINE_CAPS = DemoScenes_CapsFolded

    // Boot enters the demo's GameState_Demo_Init.
    const ENTRY_ID = GS_DEMO
    proc entry = GameState_Demo_Init
}
